SPEC §6 'Theme', 'Blink', 'Styling from outside', §7. theme values: one colour (both modes, as today) or { light => ..., dark => ... }; new keys bg, fg, muted, border, edge besides the phases; the existing colour-syntax check applies to every value, a bad one falls back to the default. blink => [phases] adds a CSS keyframe animation (no script) for g.comb.phase-<phase>; blink_seconds (default 1.2, positive number); under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce no animation, a thicker outline instead. An unknown phase name in blink is ignored. Without blink the output must not contain any animation CSS, and output without the new options stays byte-identical to before. CLI: --blink Error,Blocked, --blink-seconds, --color Key=Colour (repeatable; Key=light,dark sets both modes). POD documents the custom property names (--comb-*) and the classes as public interface. Tests: light/dark values land in the right block; surface keys; rejected colour; blink CSS present only for the named phases; reduced-motion block; determinism. Use blink for Error in examples/monitor.svg if the packed-layout card is done. Depends on the packed-layout card only for the demo.

2026-10-02 04:33 Decisions on SPEC open points. 1) theme keys are case-sensitive and exact: phases as in phases() (Error), surfaces lowercase (bg fg muted border edge); same rule as before, no second spelling to document. A light/dark hash is checked per mode; a missing or bad mode keeps the default of that mode; other hash keys are ignored. 2) blink phases: exact names from phases(), so all seven incl. Disabled and Unknown may blink (callers choice, no reason to forbid); anything else is dropped, so only names from the fixed list reach the style. Written in legend order, deduplicated: bytes independent of input order. 3) Pulse: keyframes comb-blink with only a 50 percent frame (fill-opacity .4, stroke-width size*0.07) on polygon.hex. Start and end are the cells own values, so borrowed and disabled keep their look, nothing moves, the group never fades. blink_seconds is the animation-duration (full period there and back), ease-in-out, infinite. 4) Thicker outline under reduced motion: the peak stroke width size*0.07 (normal size*0.03) with animation:none. 5) Blinking cells get their phase line in --comb-fg instead of --comb-muted: muted text on the .4 fill is about 3:1 contrast, fg about 8:1 in both modes. Static, also under reduced motion. 6) blink_seconds is written with two decimals, at least 0.01; what does not print as a plain decimal (inf, 1e30) gives 1.2. isa PositiveNum like size. 7) blink_seconds without blink changes nothing in the output.

